# FIFO Documentation

## Configuration

The FIFO uses:

```text
Data width : 8 bits
Depth      : 8 entries
```

Therefore the maximum storage capacity is:

```text
8 × 8 = 64 bits
```

## Signals

| Signal     | Direction | Description         |
| ---------- | --------- | ------------------- |
| `clk`      | Input     | System clock        |
| `rst`      | Input     | Reset               |
| `wr_en`    | Input     | Write enable        |
| `rd_en`    | Input     | Read enable         |
| `data_in`  | Input     | 8-bit input data    |
| `data_out` | Output    | Current FIFO output |
| `full`     | Output    | FIFO full flag      |
| `empty`    | Output    | FIFO empty flag     |

## Write

When:

```text
wr_en = 1
full = 0
```

the input value is stored in the FIFO.

## Read

When:

```text
rd_en = 1
empty = 0
```

the read pointer advances to the next FIFO entry.

## Status

The FIFO generates:

```text
FULL
EMPTY
```

These signals are used by the APB slave to prevent invalid accesses.
